    "recommendations": "Ensuring the single access point and extended driveway remain clear of parked vehicles and other obstructions could significantly improve apparatus entry and exit during an emergency response. Posting visible address markers at the street frontage and at the driveway entrance may assist responding units in locating the property quickly, particularly during low-visibility conditions. Maintaining adequate turning and staging space near the main building and detached structure would support simultaneous multi-unit operations. Given the limited rear access, communicating the property layout to the local fire agency in advance could facilitate pre-incident planning and improve operational effectiveness upon arrival."
